# ⚠ Zero-byte files with names like `3`, `3,`, `o.parentId` or `!!o.seating` keep
# appearing here. They are not a build artefact — they are shell redirections from
# one-liners whose quoting broke (a `>` or a `|` landing in the wrong place), and
# they have been deleted by hand twice. They are NOT ignored on purpose: an ignore
# rule would hide the mistake instead of the mess. Write a script file rather than
# a long inline command, and check `git status` before committing.
